      "key": "engineering-screening-WS3b",
      "role": "energy",
      "note": "Pump energy = volume x 9.81 x head / 3.6e6 / efficiency (kWh); diesel L = hydraulic kWh / (efficiency x 10.75 kWh/L, 38.7 MJ/L). Efficiencies: small diesel pumpset 0.15, larger diesel 0.25, electric wire-to-water 0.6 (FAO Irrigation Water Management training manuals, pump efficiency ranges). Field-operation diesel uses the mechanised-cereal 40-80 L/ha band. Reviewer to confirm against national surveys."
